<section style="padding:72px 24px 40px;"><div style="max-width:860px;margin:0 auto;"><div class="rich"><p>Torquay has grown fast, and a lot of that growth has landed on top of the old town rather than beside it. Original beach houses and holiday shacks get renovated or knocked down, and that is usually the moment asbestos turns up. Asbestos cement was used in Australian homes from the mid 1940s until the late 1980s, so anything built or extended before 1990 deserves a look before a crowbar goes near it.</p><p>We are not a removalist and we hold no licence. What we do is put you in touch with licensed asbestos removalists we work with, and their WorkSafe Victoria licence number appears on every quote. You deal with the removalist directly. If you are not certain the material is asbestos at all, start with <a href="/asbestos-testing-geelong/">a sample test</a>, because it is cheap and it settles the question. The same applies across <a href="/asbestos-removal-geelong/">Geelong</a> and the rest of the region.</p></div></div></section>
<section style="padding:0 24px 64px;"><div style="max-width:1100px;margin:0 auto;">
    <span class="kicker">What We Do in Torquay</span>
    <h2 class="section-heading" style="font-size:clamp(22px,3vw,32px);margin:0 0 28px;">Services for Torquay Properties</h2>
    <div class="feat-grid" style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,1fr);gap:20px;">
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #e3ded4;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Nunito Sans',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#0A3D5C;margin:0 0 8px;">Asbestos sample testing</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Samples go to a NATA accredited laboratory, and published Victorian rates run about $88 to $160 per sample. Most Torquay houses need three to eight, because a fence, an eaves lining and a bathroom wall sheet are three separate samples, not one.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #e3ded4;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Nunito Sans',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#0A3D5C;margin:0 0 8px;">Asbestos fence removal</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Old fibro back fences go brittle and start cracking along the bottom edge, and salt air on the coast does not help. Published Victorian figures put a whole fence at $1,000 to $3,500, with a minimum job charge of $800 to $1,500 that applies even to a short run.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #e3ded4;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Nunito Sans',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#0A3D5C;margin:0 0 8px;">Roof, eaves and shed removal</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Super Six corrugated roofing, fibro eaves and old beach house sheds are common around Torquay and Jan Juc. Victorian rates run about $40 to $120 per square metre, with a garage or small roof at $3,500 to $5,500 and a full set of eaves at $1,500 to $2,500.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #e3ded4;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Nunito Sans',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#0A3D5C;margin:0 0 8px;">Disposal that actually complies</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Asbestos is not accepted at the Torquay waste drop off or at any other Surf Coast Shire site, so it has to travel to a licensed landfill. Licensed removalists take the waste away as part of the job, wrapped and labelled the way EPA Victoria requires.</p>
      </div>
</div>
